1
00:00:01,780 --> 00:00:09,044
Welcome to MyAudioShelf. This video shows you, step by step, how to run your audiobook store.

2
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:15,237
You don’t need any technical knowledge. Just follow along, and pause the video whenever you like.

3
00:00:15,904 --> 00:00:21,751
Here is everything we’ll cover, from signing in and adding your first book, to what your listeners see.

4
00:00:24,185 --> 00:00:31,934
To manage your store, add slash admin to the end of your website address. This opens the Shelf studio sign in page.

5
00:00:32,088 --> 00:00:35,145
Type the email address of your staff account.

6
00:00:35,690 --> 00:00:40,580
Then type your password. For your security, it stays hidden as you type.

7
00:00:40,735 --> 00:00:43,105
Now click Open Shelf studio.

8
00:00:46,128 --> 00:00:54,505
The first five times you sign in, a guided tour opens by itself. It points to each part of the screen and explains what it does.

9
00:00:54,665 --> 00:00:56,885
Click Show me around to begin.

10
00:00:57,042 --> 00:01:04,271
The highlighted area is the part being explained. Click Next to move on, or Back to see the last step again.

11
00:01:04,782 --> 00:01:13,638
You can stop at any time with Skip tour, or the cross in the corner. On the first and last step, you can also choose Don’t show this guide again.

12
00:01:13,821 --> 00:01:21,429
Let’s skip it for now. A small message reminds you that the tour is always available from the Guided tour button in the left menu.

13
00:01:21,588 --> 00:01:27,700
This is your dashboard. On the left is the main menu, which takes you to every part of the studio.

14
00:01:27,855 --> 00:01:42,742
Overview is this page. Audiobooks is your catalogue. Genres organise your books. Orders shows purchases, Production enquiries holds messages from authors, Staff is your team, and Audit history is a record of every change.

15
00:01:42,896 --> 00:01:46,314
The boxes in the middle show your store at a glance.

16
00:01:46,493 --> 00:01:54,181
Paid revenue is money from completed orders. Books counts every title, and Drafts counts the books you are still preparing.

17
00:01:54,367 --> 00:02:01,723
Orders counts purchases, Enquiries counts new messages, and Trailers shows how many times previews were played.

18
00:02:01,876 --> 00:02:07,595
Subscribers counts newsletter sign ups, and Page views shows visits to your website.

19
00:02:07,792 --> 00:02:12,555
Further down are your most recent orders, and your most purchased titles.

20
00:02:12,714 --> 00:02:19,465
At the top right, View storefront opens your public website, so you can check how everything looks.

21
00:02:19,626 --> 00:02:23,816
Now, let’s add a new audiobook. Click Add an audiobook.

22
00:02:25,487 --> 00:02:34,261
The form has four sections. Book details. Cover and audio. Price, featuring and genres. And Publication.

23
00:02:34,417 --> 00:02:36,954
First, type the book’s title.

24
00:02:37,109 --> 00:02:42,548
Then the author’s name. If this author is new, they are added for you automatically.

25
00:02:42,702 --> 00:02:46,339
The narrator is optional. It is shown on the book’s page.

26
00:02:46,494 --> 00:02:51,628
Language is already set to English. Change it if your book is in another language.

27
00:02:51,781 --> 00:02:58,281
Next, write a description. This is what listeners read before they buy, so make it inviting.

28
00:02:58,437 --> 00:03:07,542
Production style describes the recording. Narrated is a single voice. Immersive adds music and sound. Full cast uses several actors.

29
00:03:07,698 --> 00:03:09,754
Now for the cover and audio.

30
00:03:09,915 --> 00:03:18,033
Under Cover artwork, click Choose file and pick your cover image. JPG, PNG or WebP pictures work best.

31
00:03:18,204 --> 00:03:26,417
Under Audio preview, choose a short sample of up to sixty seconds. Anyone can play this on your website, for free.

32
00:03:26,572 --> 00:03:34,921
For the full recording you have two choices. Upload the whole audiobook as one file under Full audiobook, or add it chapter by chapter.

33
00:03:35,076 --> 00:03:39,098
We’ll add chapters. Type the first chapter’s title here.

34
00:03:39,256 --> 00:03:42,031
Then choose that chapter’s audio file.

35
00:03:42,186 --> 00:03:47,694
Now the price. Type it in pounds, for example nine pounds ninety nine.

36
00:03:47,849 --> 00:03:51,854
Tick at least one genre, so listeners can find the book.

37
00:03:52,008 --> 00:04:01,304
Under Publication status, Draft keeps the book hidden while you work on it. Published puts it on your website. Archived takes it off the website.

38
00:04:01,459 --> 00:04:09,110
Show on homepage lists the book on your home page. Main homepage book makes it the large book at the very top of the home page.

39
00:04:09,273 --> 00:04:14,033
We’ll keep it as a Draft for now. Scroll down and click Save audiobook.

40
00:04:16,384 --> 00:04:23,115
The green message at the top confirms it is saved. Each uploaded file now says Uploaded, with its size.

41
00:04:23,271 --> 00:04:29,861
Let’s add the second chapter the same way. Type its title, choose its audio file, and save.

42
00:04:30,973 --> 00:04:42,348
Your chapters are listed here, in the order listeners will hear them. Move up and Move down change the order, and Remove deletes a chapter. You can only remove chapters while the book is a Draft.

43
00:04:42,501 --> 00:04:50,998
Before going live, click Preview at the top. It shows exactly how the book’s page will look to listeners. Buying is switched off in preview.

44
00:04:51,157 --> 00:04:54,230
Click Back to admin to return to the studio.

45
00:04:54,385 --> 00:05:00,546
Open the book again with Edit. When everything is ready, change Publication status to Published.

46
00:05:00,702 --> 00:05:02,759
Then click Save audiobook.

47
00:05:03,357 --> 00:05:07,394
That’s it. The book is now live on your website and ready to buy.

48
00:05:07,574 --> 00:05:13,322
Sometimes you want to announce a book before it is ready to sell. That is what Featured is for.

49
00:05:13,476 --> 00:05:18,262
Add a new audiobook, and fill in the title, the author and a description.

50
00:05:23,490 --> 00:05:26,810
Upload a cover. You don’t need any audio yet.

51
00:05:26,966 --> 00:05:28,678
Leave the price empty.

52
00:05:28,864 --> 00:05:34,625
Tick Featured. Because there is no price, the book’s price tag will say Coming soon.

53
00:05:34,782 --> 00:05:39,537
Choose a genre, set Publication status to Published, and save.

54
00:05:40,781 --> 00:05:45,491
The message confirms the book is on the Featured page, as Coming soon.

55
00:05:45,647 --> 00:05:54,463
Here is the Featured page on your website. Every featured book without a price is listed here with a Coming soon tag, and nobody can buy it yet.

56
00:05:54,617 --> 00:05:59,152
When you are ready to sell, go back to the book, and type a price.

57
00:06:02,808 --> 00:06:13,386
If anything is missing, the studio tells you exactly what. Here, a book on sale needs a preview and the full audio. Click any message to jump straight to that field.

58
00:06:13,549 --> 00:06:17,327
Choose the preview and the full audiobook, and save again.

59
00:06:20,009 --> 00:06:27,079
Now the book is on sale. It leaves the Featured page by itself, and appears on the bookshelf with its price.

60
00:06:27,910 --> 00:06:31,533
Click Audiobooks in the menu to see all of your titles.

61
00:06:31,688 --> 00:06:34,593
Search for any book by its title here.

62
00:06:35,337 --> 00:06:42,950
Reset clears the search. These tabs show all titles, only Featured books, or only books that are Coming soon.

63
00:06:43,106 --> 00:06:51,607
Each row shows the book’s status, its price and its collections. Edit opens the book’s form, and Preview shows its public page.

64
00:06:53,306 --> 00:07:00,261
Genres help listeners find books on your website. To add one, type its name, and click Add genre.

65
00:07:00,415 --> 00:07:05,639
The new genre is ready straight away, in the book form and in your website’s filters.

66
00:07:07,506 --> 00:07:11,268
When someone buys a book, the order appears under Orders.

67
00:07:11,422 --> 00:07:17,803
Click an order to open it. You can see the total, the payment details, and the books that were bought.

68
00:07:17,958 --> 00:07:25,996
Under Listening access, you control who can play the book. Every change needs a short reason, which is saved in the audit history.

69
00:07:26,152 --> 00:07:33,421
Revoke access stops the listener from playing the book, for example after a refund. Restore access gives it back.

70
00:07:33,577 --> 00:07:40,673
If a listener loses their email, type a reason and click Email new listening link. A fresh link is sent to them.

71
00:07:42,338 --> 00:07:47,828
Authors and publishers who contact you through your website appear under Production enquiries.

72
00:07:47,989 --> 00:07:56,440
Each enquiry shows the person’s details, their project and their message. If they attached a manuscript, you can download it here.

73
00:07:56,595 --> 00:08:02,074
As you work with them, change the status. For example, from New to Reviewing.

74
00:08:02,228 --> 00:08:06,291
Add private notes for your team, and click Save enquiry.

75
00:08:09,196 --> 00:08:12,904
Under Staff, you can give your team their own sign in.

76
00:08:13,058 --> 00:08:22,518
Owners can do everything. Editors manage books, genres and enquiries. Support staff manage orders, listening access and enquiries.

77
00:08:22,674 --> 00:08:28,612
To add someone, type their email address and a starting password of at least twelve characters.

78
00:08:28,766 --> 00:08:31,871
Choose their role, and click Add staff member.

79
00:08:32,025 --> 00:08:37,669
If someone leaves, click Disable. They are signed out everywhere, straight away.

80
00:08:39,372 --> 00:08:49,202
Audit history keeps a record of every important action, with the time, who did it, and what changed. It is useful if you ever need to check what happened.

81
00:08:49,366 --> 00:08:54,310
Now let’s see your website the way listeners do. Click View storefront.

82
00:08:54,479 --> 00:09:00,621
The home page opens with your main book. Visitors can play its preview, or buy it straight away.

83
00:09:00,777 --> 00:09:04,344
The menu at the top leads to every part of your website.

84
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:09,400
Hover over Services to see what you offer. These details are for reading only.

85
00:09:09,556 --> 00:09:15,698
Hover over Discover for your company pages, such as About, Our services and Innovation.

86
00:09:16,730 --> 00:09:19,929
The bookshelf lists every book that is on sale.

87
00:09:20,084 --> 00:09:26,505
Listeners can search, and filter by genre, language, length, price and more.

88
00:09:26,669 --> 00:09:30,072
The Featured page shows the books that are coming soon.

89
00:09:30,246 --> 00:09:35,140
Clicking a book opens its page, with the cover, the price and the description.

90
00:09:35,295 --> 00:09:40,753
Listen to the preview plays the free sample, in a small player at the bottom of the screen.

91
00:09:41,770 --> 00:09:44,720
Add to cart puts the book in the listener’s cart.

92
00:09:45,233 --> 00:09:53,505
The cart shows their books and the total. They type their email address and click Continue to checkout. Payment is handled securely by Stripe.

93
00:09:53,666 --> 00:10:01,703
After paying, they receive an email with a private link to listen to, or download, their audiobook. No account is needed.

94
00:10:01,861 --> 00:10:08,421
My purchases is where returning listeners ask for a new listening link, using the same email address.

95
00:10:08,576 --> 00:10:15,207
These buttons switch the book opening sounds on or off, and switch your website between dark and light colours.

96
00:10:16,302 --> 00:10:21,122
At the bottom of every page are links to your pages, and to your social media.

97
00:10:21,314 --> 00:10:27,226
Let’s go back to the studio. When you have finished, click Sign out at the bottom of the menu.

98
00:10:30,611 --> 00:10:40,939
And that’s everything. Remember: save as a Draft while you work, choose Published to go live, and leave the price empty with Featured ticked to announce a book as Coming soon.

99
00:10:41,093 --> 00:10:48,223
If you ever need a reminder, the Guided tour button in the studio menu walks you through every page. Happy publishing!
